  abstract={The current trend toward online and remote workplaces has left a severe requirement in secure and effective attendance management systems. This study proposes an IoT Security-Enhanced Attendance Tracking Unit intended to guarantee real-time authentication, data integrity as well as scalability in the management of remote work forces. The suggested model uses Min-max Normalization as a preprocessing method and Principal component analysis to reduce dimensions, which renders it more computationally efficient. The high accuracy of a Gradient Boosted Decision Trees classifier, which is implemented in TensorFlow Extended, is the verification of the identity of employees and the prediction of their attendance. The experimental findings prove that the model has an accuracy of 97.8 which is much better than the traditional RFID and cloud-based systems. Privacy protection and the quick response time are guaranteed by the merging of reliable communication strategies and smart data analysis. In general, the framework presented gives a powerful, scalable, and intelligent solution to the present-day workforce monitoring in a distributed organizational setting.},
