  abstract={Network perimeters are no longer static boundaries; they are porous, software-defined edges. Traditional firewalls, reliant on static rules, often fail to intercept sophisticated, behavior-based cyber-attacks, creating a critical need for security systems that combine deep packet inspection with dynamic intelligence. This work proposes a lightweight, robust Intrusion Detection System (IDS) optimized explicitly for cloud-native environments. By merging real-time packet sniffing with a Random Forest classification engine, the system moves beyond signature matching to identify threats based on behavioral anomalies. The architecture leverages Kubernetes DaemonSets to ensure uniform node-level monitoring and utilizes a decoupled FastAPI backend for centralized alert management. Theoretical analysis of the system’s algorithmic complexity reveals high efficiency even in high-traffic scenarios, while empirical results demonstrate that the system maintains low latency (sub-200ms) and high detection accuracy (98.4%) across distributed clusters.},
